Subject: Clear scratch fields on short header reads

Local follow-up to the alignment fix: header_read returns before copying
a short read. Reset every numeric scratch destination so an earlier field
cannot become a failed field. This preserves 1.2.2 zero values for the new
scratch users and prevents their data reaching prior scratch users too.
The internal test uses benign cached bytes plus a virtual error/EOF/short-read
callback for every numeric specifier and both byte orders.

